      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI'm zeroing in on a Python script, `profile_claims.py`, and have decided to start with Google's People API. This approach sets a concrete focus for fetching and standardizing federated user profile claims. I'm choosing a popular and well-documented API for this purpose.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI'm now outlining the structure of `profile_claims.py`. I'll create a function that takes an access token, calls the Google People API, and returns normalized claims. I'll include `google-auth` and `google-api-python-client`. Placeholder credentials will be used initially.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865306797,
          "start": 1789865304500
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4921b4001dcD9k6OXg6SF3a",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc491c79001SdWN8TbCEIhaZA",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b6e39affexANxjIy7Wb3aLl",
