      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the OAuth Flow**\n\nI'm starting to sketch out the `oauth_callback.py` file. The primary goal is to manage the OAuth/OIDC callback, particularly token exchange. Google seems like a solid choice for the initial implementation, as it's well-documented and widely supported. I'll need to figure out how to best integrate that provider into the program.\n\n\n**Implementing the Callback Handler**\n\nI'm now diving into the `oauth_callback.py` structure. The plan's coming together, with code taking shape for extracting the authorization code from the request and exchanging it. I'm focusing on Google's OAuth2 API, and getting environment variables for credentials. I'm leaning toward getting these from `os.environ`. I'm going to define the function to handle the callback; the next step is the token exchange itself.\n\n\n**Structuring the Code**\n\nI'm now focusing on the Python file's skeleton. I'm building a simple framework with placeholder values. I'm importing `requests` for token exchanges. Google's token endpoint is hardcoded as `GOOGLE_TOKEN_URL = \"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\"`. I'll use environment variables for the client ID and secret. The OAuth logic, using Google's API, will be the heart of the callback handler.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865301379,
          "start": 1789865297692
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc49071c001KiBmQRMzl6aMLc",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4901f0001ra8goMtbPutp5A",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b6fe21ffe6BC4YJn8zLooiL",
      "time_created": 1789865297692,
      "time_updated": 1789865301380
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tBoI8AUGDTSHuvFZ",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport requests\nimport json\n\ndef handle_oauth_callback(authorization_code: str, redirect_uri: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles the OAuth/OIDC callback, exchanging an authorization code for tokens.\n    Uses Google as the concrete external provider.\n    \"\"\"\n    google_client_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\")\n    google_client_secret = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET\")\n    google_token_url = \"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\" # Google's token endpoint\n\n    if not google_client_id or not google_client_secret:\n        raise ValueError(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET environment variables must be set.\")\n\n    token_payload = {\n        \"client_id\": google_client_id,\n        \"client_secret\": google_client_secret,\n        \"code\": authorization_code,\n        \"redirect_uri\": redirect_uri,\n        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n    }\n\n    try:\n        response = requests.post(google_token_url, data=token_payload)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n        tokens = response.json()\n        return tokens\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        print(f\"Error exchanging authorization code for tokens: {e}\")\n        raise\n\n",
            "filePath": "oauth_callback.py"
          },
